pw_lod_bench.cpp / pw_lod_bench.h in this directory are carried byte for byte
from the PocketWorld splat A/B bench (pw_splat_ab_bench Sources/lod/ @ b792d57,
sha256 50af752c1372aa881ff4dcc2b92e5fb0579daa36afc71567859938d21867b6c9 and
d5a349a2dfd0721a19a5fb345515ddcd8b85b1143d8b19a95e753edebfaf780e) so that the
device measurement (plan M1, pwlod_run) runs the exact code measured on the Mac.
They are not edited, so the notice required by the upstream they transliterate
is given here instead of in their header.

The WGSL in pw_lod_bench.cpp (numberOfOnes, isBitSet, getLOD, the adaptive point
size) and its visible-node table / LodByte are transliterated from Potree
(https://github.com/potree/potree @ 5636cd471d9eb464969e758be45c44d7613d3859:
src/materials/shaders/pointcloud.vs, src/PointCloudOctree.js), used under this
